{"comment":"Shard map for the iOS test suite (issue #134). The guard (scripts/check-ios-test-shards.py) fails if the XCTestCase classes and test methods found in the Swift sources do not match this map exactly: every class assigned exactly once, no stale entries, and for a class split by method (MealRecipeFlowsTests) every test method assigned to exactly one shard. The unit job runs the whole PitTechTests target; its classes are enumerated so additions and renames are caught instead of drifting silently. UI entries are xcodebuild -only-testing suffixes: a bare class name runs the whole class; Class/method runs one method. UI shards are balanced by measured durations from prototype run 39701802389 (2026-10-21): flows-a/flows-b split MealRecipeFlowsTests' 3,353s of test time into 1,668s / 1,685s; ui-2 carries 2,453s; ui-3 carries 1,883s. Each shard runs on its own runner with exactly one simulator (the one-simulator-per-host constraint stands).","uiShards":{"flows-a":["MealRecipeFlowsTests/testPrivateSyncConflictReviewResolvesOfflineAtBothTextSizes","MealRecipeFlowsTests/testAccountDeletionReviewRecoveryAndCompletionAtBothTextSizes","MealRecipeFlowsTests/testAnonymousReportRecoveryAndPublisherBlockAtBothTextSizes","MealRecipeFlowsTests/testLocalJournalRemovalConfirmationAtBothTextSizes","MealRecipeFlowsTests/testRecordedCookImportDoesNotSaveRecipesAtStandardAndLargeText","MealRecipeFlowsTests/testCodeImportRejectsForeignLinksBeforeAnyImportAtBothTextSizes","MealRecipeFlowsTests/testBetaConnectionOnboardingRejectsInsecureServersAtStandardAndLargeText"],"flows-b":["MealRecipeFlowsTests/testSelectedPublicationPreviewAndCookbookChangesRequireSeparateConfirmationsAtBothTextSizes","MealRecipeFlowsTests/testOneGuideToggleControlsAllSectionsAndPersistsAtStandardAndLargeText","MealRecipeFlowsTests/testAccountCodeFlowAndSignOutKeepLocalCookbookAtBothTextSizes","MealRecipeFlowsTests/testSignedOutDiscoverySavesPrivateCopiesAndStartsANewMealAtBothTextSizes","MealRecipeFlowsTests/t